{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.deleted_word_not_two_components","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.deleted_word_not_two_components","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L190-L198","doc":"**The bridge fails.** The naive deletion's closure has one component, while\na 2-component sublink of a 3-component link must have two. So the trefoil it\nexhibits is not a sublink of the nucleon, and cannot host a pion.\n\nStated via the permutation because that is what the component count reads: the\nBorromean word returns the identity (`borromean_perm_id`, 3 fixed points, 3\ncomponents), the deleted word returns a transposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.deleted_word_perm_is_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.deleted_word_perm_is_swap","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L185-L188","doc":"The naively strand-deleted word `(σ₀⁻¹)³` closes with the strands\n**exchanged** — a single 2-cycle, hence a **one**-component closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.meson_mechanism_vanishes_on_nucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.meson_mechanism_vanishes_on_nucleon","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L148-L163","doc":"**The meson mechanism cannot be the intra-nucleon one.** For any `F` that\nvanishes on zero linking, if `F` is nonzero on the meson carrier (the Hopf\nlink, `lk ≠ 0`) then it is zero on every pair of the nucleon carrier.\n\nSo an `E_EM` transported from the meson sector along pairwise linking is\nidentically zero inside the nucleon — it cannot reach the ≈ 0.8 MeV comparator,\nand it cannot distinguish the proton from the neutron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.pairwise_functional_cannot_separate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.pairwise_functional_cannot_separate","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L113-L125","doc":"**The prune.** Any functional of the pairwise linking data alone takes the\nsame value on the proton braid as on the 3-component unlink.\n\nSo an `E_EM` ansatz built from pairwise linking cannot distinguish them; if it\nvanishes on the unlink — as a self-energy must — it vanishes on the proton, and\ncannot reach the ≈ 0.8 MeV comparator. The search should go to `μ̄₁₂₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.hopf_crossSum_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.hopf_crossSum_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L109-L111","doc":"**The control.** The same simulator returns a nonzero sum on the Hopf link,\nso the Borromean zeros are a fact about that word and not about this file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.borromean_crossSum_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.borromean_crossSum_zero","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L102-L107","doc":"All three pairwise signed crossing sums vanish on the Borromean braid,\nhence all three linking numbers are `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.borromean_perm_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.borromean_perm_id","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L98-L100","doc":"The Borromean word closes to a genuine **three**-component link: the strand\nordering returns to the identity, so no two components have been merged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.hopfWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.hopfWord","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L95-L96","doc":"The Hopf link `σ₀²`, used as the control. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.borWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.borWord","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L92-L93","doc":"The corpus's Borromean presentation `(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.crossSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.crossSum","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L81-L90","doc":"Signed crossing sum between strands `s` and `t` along a braid word. Each\nletter `(i, e)` exchanges the strands at positions `i`, `i+1` and contributes\n`e` to the pair it exchanges. The linking number is half this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.finalPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.finalPerm","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L76-L79","doc":"The strand ordering after reading the whole word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.swapAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.swapAt","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L70-L74","doc":"Exchange the entries at positions `i` and `i+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.Letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking.Letter","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanPairwiseLinking.lean#L67-L68","doc":"A braid letter: the generator index `i`, and the sign of the crossing. ","signatureChunk":0}]}